# haseen's vendor terminal preference for xdg-terminal-exec, the tool a
# desktop entry with Terminal=true, GTK's "Open in Terminal" and flea's
# terminal action go through when it is installed (it comes only from
# [omarchy]; haseen's own yazi and nvim handlers do not need it).
#
# Adapted from Omarchy default/xdg-terminal-exec/hyprland-xdg-terminals.list
# (MIT, Copyright (c) David Heinemeier Hansson).
#
# The file name matters: xdg-terminal-exec looks for
# "<lowercased $XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP>-xdg-terminals.list" before the plain
# "xdg-terminals.list" in each $XDG_DATA_DIRS/xdg-terminal-exec/ directory
# (/usr/bin/xdg-terminal-exec:156-162). Under uwsm + Hyprland
# XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP is "Hyprland", hence hyprland-.
#
# This is the vendor fallback. The user's own choice lives in
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xdg-terminals.list, which is read first; the 50-handlers
# seed creates it from $TERMINAL and `haseen setup default terminal` rewrites
# it.
#
# The first entry that exists and is valid wins.
foot.desktop
